================================================================
CRITICAL (2026-09-09, 21:00): THE LLM STAGE NEVER RAN. ALL RUNS
BEFORE THIS POINT ARE DETERMINISTIC-FALLBACK RUNS.
================================================================
The first real campaign (19 configs, 9 completed) produced 0 findings.
The reason was NOT the targets and NOT Python 3.11. Both LLM roles in
the pipeline were dead, silently, while the logs looked healthy.

(a) SANITIZER SELECTION -- json parse bug in src/llm.py
    select_sanitizers() did:
        content = response.content.strip().strip("```json").strip("```").strip()
        json.loads(content)
    str.strip(chars) removes a CHARACTER SET, not a substring, so
    .strip("```json") strips any of ` j s o n from both ends; and
    nothing there survives prose outside the fence. llama3.1:8b returns
    correct JSON wrapped in an explanation + a bare ``` fence, so every
    call raised "Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0)".
    fuzzer.py caught it and logged "Falling back to default sanitizers".
    => RQ2/RQ3 had NO evidence behind them.

(b) SEED GENERATION -- src/seed_bank/ was deleted in commit 87d8602
    ("latest edit", which also removed src/predefined_seeds/,
    dictionaries/ and configs/). _load_seed_bank() returned {} so
    generate_seeds() short-circuited to _local_fallback_mapping() on
    every tool. Restored from b1b657e: path_traversal, sql_injection,
    ssrf_url, wildcards, xml_bomb, xss_markdown.
    >> STILL MISSING: src/predefined_seeds/ (the create_pdf/create_docx/
       create_zip tool-calling path writes there; file_manager.py reads
       "predefined_seed:<name>"). Decide whether to restore it too or to
       drop the binary-seed claim from the paper.

(c) 'NoneType' object is not callable -- llm.py caught ImportError and
    set ChatOpenAI = None, so a missing/half-installed langchain_openai
    surfaced 400 lines later as a TypeError. Now raises at construction
    with the original ImportError attached.

FIXES APPLIED (src/llm.py):
  - _extract_json(): fence-aware, prose-tolerant, brace-balanced with
    string-literal + escape awareness; _coerce_text() flattens
    content-block lists. Unit-tested against the verbatim llama3.1:8b
    reply from the failing log, plus 9 other shapes.
  - select_sanitizers(): 3 attempts (TOFU_LLM_JSON_ATTEMPTS), each
    re-asking with a sharper instruction; backend JSON mode via
    response_format={"type":"json_object"} (TOFU_LLM_JSON_MODE=0 to
    disable); hallucinated sanitizer names are dropped AND counted; the
    old code also fell off the end returning None when the shape check
    failed -- now always returns or raises.
  - greppable markers: LLM_SELECTION_OK / LLM_SELECTION_FAILED /
    LLM_SEEDGEN_OK / LLM_SEEDGEN_FALLBACK.
  - backup at src/llm.py.bak-preLLMfix

FIXES APPLIED (eval/run_eval.py):
  - every run record now carries llm_selection (ok|failed|unknown),
    llm_n_selected, llm_n_dropped, llm_seeds (ok|fallback|unknown),
    llm_n_seeds.
  - end-of-run summary prints the LLM-stage histogram over the WHOLE
    index and shouts if selection never succeeded once.

QUARANTINED: eval/state/quarantine-pre-llmfix/ holds the 9 old run
records, their logs, the bogus-rc1 batch, the coverage CSVs and the old
fuzz_corpus, plus a WHY.md. NONE of it is evidence about ToFu.

