--- BUG 5: THE SEED CORPUS IS WRITTEN WITH LLM TOOL-CALL ENVELOPES, NOT WITH
--- TOOL ARGUMENTS. THE PARSER FIX IS CORRECT AND STILL GETS BYPASSED. ---

Verbatim from disk, eval/corpora/AppiumTestDistribution__mcp-appium-gestures__
generate-double-tap-code/seed_1.json (207 bytes):

  {"name": "create_json", "parameters": {"filename": "test_case.json",
   "json_content": "{\"language\": \"java\", \"useElement\": false,
   \"elementId\": \"element2\", \"x\": 0, \"y\": 0, \"pauseDuration\": 0}"}}

All 12 seed files have this shape. The tool's schema is
{language, useElement, elementId, x, y, pauseDuration}. The seed's TOP-LEVEL
keys are "name" and "parameters". input_parser._try_parse_json requires
matched > 0 against the schema properties (input_parser.py:88), so matched=0,
parsed_successfully=False, and parse() correctly falls through to the
FuzzedDataProvider branch -- which re-reads those bytes through
ConsumeUnicodeNoSurrogates. That is where the mojibake comes back:

  log line 114: -> Faulty Input : {'language': 'javascript', 'useElement': True,
    'elementId': '慮敭㨢∠牣慥整機潳≮...', 'x': 0.0, 'y': 0.0, 'pauseDuration': 0.0}
  '慮敭㨢∠牣慥整機潳≮' is UTF-16LE for  name": "create_json

So the mojibake from the pre-parserfix quarantine is BACK, from a different
cause. Fix 3 (JSON-first) did its job; the input it is handed cannot match any
schema, so there is nothing for it to honour.

MECHANISM (all four links in the log, lines 43-62 and 111):
 1. The LLM made 12 correct create_json tool calls. Their ARGUMENTS are right:
      {"language": "javascript", "useElement": true, "elementId": "element1",
       "x": 10, "y": 20, "pauseDuration": 200}
 2. create_json wrote those to src/predefined_seeds/test_case_N.json and
    returned the reference string "predefined_seed:test_case_N.json".
 3. On attempt=2 the model emitted, as its FINAL JSON array, an array of its
    own tool-call envelopes rather than an array of tool-argument objects.
    _extract_json(expect=list) accepts it -- it IS a list -- and llm.py:528
    logs LLM_SEEDGEN_OK n_seeds=12. The marker reports SUCCESS over seeds that
    cannot match any schema. Same failure family as bugs 1-4: a healthy log
    line over a dead stage.
 4. libFuzzer: "seed corpus: files: 12 min: 207b max: 227b" then collapses to
    corp: 1/207b, because all 12 envelopes drive identical coverage.

CONTRAST -- the path CAN work. The excel run's seeds are correctly shaped:
  eval/corpora/ArchimedesCrypto__excel-reader-mcp__get_cell/seed_0.json =
  {"filePath": "predefined_seed:example.xlsx", "sheet": "Sheet1", "cell": "A1"}
Keys match the schema. So this is per-tool/per-reply, which makes it exactly
the kind of bug that a campaign averages into a plausible-looking result.

--- CONSEQUENCE: THE JS COVERAGE ACCEPTANCE TEST IS NOT YET ANSWERED ---
The appium log has only 5 libFuzzer status lines, all identical:
    #4  pulse  cov: 2761 ft: 2761 corp: 1/207b exec/s: 0 rss: 566Mb
    #32 pulse  cov: 2761 ft: 2761 corp: 1/207b lim: 207 exec/s: 0 rss: 566Mb
(a) cov: did not increase. (b) corp: did not grow past 1. (c) exec/s still 0.
DO NOT read this as "Fix 2 failed". The run was driven by ONE 207-byte corpus
entry of ToFu's own tool-call JSON against a pure string-templating code
generator. There was nothing to discover. The test must be re-run on a corpus
that actually varies, on a tool that branches. Until then Fix 2 is UNTESTED,
not refuted.

--- SIDE EFFECT: RUNS WRITE INTO THE TRACKED SOURCE TREE ---
src/predefined_seeds/ held 36 files at b1b657e (git ls-tree). It now holds 50.
The extra 14 are test_case*.json written BY the run at 01:14/01:16 via the
create_json @tool. Every run appends there, all runs share the directory, and
it is a restored source asset. Cross-run contamination + dirty git state.

--- SMALLER THINGS FOUND IN THE DIFF (none fixed, none urgent) ---
 * js_runner.py: on index-space exhaustion the aliasing uses hash(cov_item).
   Python string hashing is randomised per process unless PYTHONHASHSEED is
   set, so the aliasing -- and therefore the coverage numbers -- would differ
   between runs. In a codebase that just pinned temperature and seed for
   exactly this reason, use a stable digest (zlib.crc32 / hashlib) instead.
   Only bites past 10000 distinct JS coverage items, and it warns loudly.
 * fake_coverage.trigger() is now a 10000-branch linear if-chain (was 2000),
   so reaching a high slot costs ~5x more comparisons per item than before.
   The per-call delta set is far smaller than the old cumulative set, so net
   throughput should still improve a lot -- but exec/s is the thing to watch,
   not assume, in the re-run.
 * llm.py select_sanitizers: the retry loop drops json_object mode after the
   FIRST exception of any kind, including an ordinary parse failure that had
   nothing to do with the backend rejecting response_format. Cosmetic.
 * llm.py generate_seeds: LLM_SEEDGEN_OK is logged for n_seeds=0 as well, and
   an empty list is returned WITHOUT falling back to _local_fallback_mapping.
   A run could legitimately record llm_seeds=ok with zero seeds.
 * All 3 records in runs.jsonl have budget/model/temperature = null. They were
   rebuilt by --reparse, which cannot recover provenance. None of the three is
   usable as evidence regardless of the above.
 * MongoDB reporter floods the log: 62 x "[MongoDB] Failed to log vulnerability
   ... localhost:27017 Connection refused", each with a 2s timeout. That is
   ~124s of the appium run's 540.4s wall clock spent on a DB nobody is running.
   Disable the Mongo sink for campaign runs or the budget accounting is wrong.
 * requirements.txt is now a full pip freeze of the venv (60 pins, includes
   pytest/pyflakes). Good for reproducibility; note atheris==3.0.0 will not
   install cleanly off this Mac.
 * fuzz_corpus/ at the repo root is leftover from before Fix 5 (--corpus-dir).
   Its seed_0.json is excel-shaped. Untracked junk; safe to delete.
 * `python3` on Ananto's PATH is 3.10.11, not the 3.11.15 venv. Every command
   in HANDOFF section 4 and eval/README.md says `python3 eval/...`, which will
   fail (atheris needs dis.Positions). Use .venv/bin/python everywhere.
 * Test count: .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q gives 67 passed, 0 skipped
   -- not the "66 passed, 1 skipped" that CLAUDE.md and HANDOFF section 14
   state as the gate. The previously-skipped test now runs. Update the gate.

