--- 2026-09-10, later: BUG 5 FIXED (Ananto signed off), overnight script built ---
src/llm.py    new _validate_seeds(). generate_seeds now validates BEFORE it
              declares success: a seed is kept iff it is a dict sharing at
              least one key with the schema's declared properties -- the SAME
              predicate input_parser._try_parse_json gates on (matched > 0), so
              "accepted here" means "honoured there". Rejects are logged as
              LLM_SEEDGEN_REJECTED with counts + the offending keys; if nothing
              survives it raises into the existing retry loop and ultimately
              falls back to _local_fallback_mapping. LLM_SEEDGEN_OK now carries
              tool=, n_seeds= (kept only) and n_rejected=, and can no longer be
              logged for an empty list.
              *** THIS IS A MEASUREMENT CHANGE: envelope-shaped seeds no longer
              enter the corpus. Signed off 2026-09-10. Item 14 closed. ***
src/fuzzer.py MongoVulnerabilityReporter was unconditional while
              FuzzerConfig.export_mongo (default False) was ignored. With no
              mongod, every finding cost a 2s serverSelectionTimeoutMS -- ~124s
              of the appium run's 540.4s. Now gated on config.export_mongo.
