OVERNIGHT CAMPAIGN 2026-09-10 01:40-06:51 -- ZERO FUZZING EXECUTIONS
gemma4:12b arm. Diagnosed, root causes confirmed against the live daemon.
================================================================

WHAT THE NIGHT PRODUCED
  prepare : 14 prepared / 44 skipped of 58  -> 173 configs
  campaign: 46 runs attempted, 46 TIMED OUT at 780s, 0 alerts, 0 signatures
  runs that reached libFuzzer: 0 of 47.  Every gemma4 log ends at
    "[LLM] Generation of smart seed corpus for '<tool>'".
  llm_selection over the 47: failed 43, ok 2, unknown 2.
  ~5h10m of wall clock spent entirely inside LLM calls.
  Log: eval/state/overnight_20260910_013957.log

The harness behaved correctly throughout. It recorded 46 honest failures
rather than 46 healthy-looking zeroes. That is the audit working.

ROOT CAUSE 1 -- OLLAMA SERVES gemma4:12b WITH A 4096-TOKEN CONTEXT
  Verbatim from eval/runs/api7__apisix-mcp__create_route.log:
    sanitizer-selection attempt 1/3 failed: Could not parse response content as
    the length limit was reached - CompletionUsage(completion_tokens=2045,
    prompt_tokens=2051, total_tokens=4096, ...)
  2051 + 2045 = 4096 EXACTLY. Confirmed twice against the live daemon, not
  inferred:
    curl /api/ps            -> "context_length": 4096
    llama-server argv       -> ... -c 4096 -np 1 ...
  `ollama serve --help` documents OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH as "default:
  4k/32k/256k based on VRAM". On a 16 GB M2 Pro with a 12B resident it picks
  4k. gemma4:12b's NATIVE context is 262144 (`ollama show`).
  The selection prompt is ~2051 tokens because it inlines all 72 sanitizer
  names + descriptions. That leaves ~2045 for a reply that must carry
  selected_sanitizers AND a rules object with on_trigger +
  expected_fallback_values per sanitizer. It truncates mid-JSON.
  Attempts 2 and 3 then append the parse error to an already-2051-token
  prompt and come back EMPTY.

ROOT CAUSE 2 -- gemma4 IS A THINKING MODEL AND ITS REASONING EATS THE BUDGET
  `ollama show gemma4:12b` lists capability "thinking". A direct probe returned
  a message object with a SEPARATE reasoning field alongside content:
    "content":"{\"ok\":true}",
    "reasoning":"The user wants a specific JSON response: `{\"ok\":true}`. ..."
  Reasoning tokens are billed against completion_tokens. With only ~2045 left
  under root cause 1, gemma4 spends them thinking and returns an EMPTY content
  string -- which is precisely the "empty LLM response" in attempts 2 and 3.
  The two causes compound; fixing context alone may not be enough.

ROOT CAUSE 3 -- THROUGHPUT ON THIS MACHINE IS NOT VIABLE AS CONFIGURED
  A 25-token prompt / 51-token completion took 246.2 SECONDS end to end.
  A later short call returned HTTP 000 after 36s. Meanwhile:
    memory free 13%, pageouts 842139, load avg 2.89
    llama-server resident at size_vram 8046205991 (8.0 GB) on a 16 GB machine
    Chrome and Claude both running and in the top-5 CPU consumers
  Part of the 246s is an 8 GB cold load (expires_at had just lapsed), but a
  warm re-probe could not be completed cleanly either. Treat gemma4:12b as
  UNMEASURED on throughput here, not as measured-slow -- but do not launch
  another campaign until a warm tokens/sec figure exists.

SUSPECT, NOT CONFIRMED -- WRONG CHAT TEMPLATE
  The llama-server argv contains:  --no-jinja --chat-template chatml
  i.e. Ollama is serving gemma4 with a GENERIC ChatML template rather than
  gemma4's own. If that is real and not just how Ollama 0.33.3 spells it
  internally, the model is being prompted in a format it was not tuned for,
  which independently degrades instruction-following and would explain empty
  replies. VERIFY before blaming the model for poor selection precision --
  publishing "gemma4:12b selects badly" off a template mismatch would be the
  same class of error as the temperature-0.7 anecdote.

HARNESS PROBLEMS THIS EXPOSED (none fixed yet)
  a) A DEAD RUN COSTS budget+600s REGARDLESS OF --time. run_eval.py:172 uses
     communicate(timeout=budget+600), so at --time 180 a run that cannot even
     select sanitizers still burns 780s -- 4.3x the budget. 46 x 780s IS the
     lost night. Needs a fail-fast: if LLM_SELECTION_FAILED and seed generation
     has not produced a corpus within ~60s, abort the run.
  b) budget IS NULL IN ALL 50 RECORDS. llm_model is recorded, budget is not
     (run_eval.py:63 area). A3 needs it.
  c) 15 ORPHANED node MCP SERVERS still resident, ages up to 14h52m. NINE of
     them are under the PRE-RENAME path /Users/.../pseclab/toolfuzzer/, so
     they predate the rename and have outlived several campaigns; six are
     under ToFu/, oldest 6h41m. The start_new_session+killpg fix only covers
     the timeout path of the CURRENT harness. Kill them before any timing
     measurement:  pkill -f coverage_wrapper.js

