--- 2026-09-10 07:40 -- WHY THE 32k FIX MADE IT WORSE, AND THE REAL FIX ---
Smoke run at ctx=32768 was WORSE than at 4096: 720.1s timeout with ZERO
completed HTTP requests (eval/runs/api7__apisix-mcp__delete_plugin_metadata.log
ends at "Retrying request in 0.44s"). Raising the context did not fix the LLM
stage, it removed the accidental brake.

MEASURED WARM THROUGHPUT (memory free 82%, orphans killed, ctx 32768):
    prompt  3016 tok in 19.8s  = 152 tok/s prefill
    gen      512 tok in 29.3s  = 17.5 tok/s
The model is NOT slow. 3000-token prompt + 512 generated = 49s.

ROOT CAUSE: gemma4:12b is a thinking model and nothing capped it. At 17.5
tok/s, ~12k reasoning tokens is ~11 minutes for ONE call. At 4096 context the
thinking was truncated at ~2045 tokens ("length limit was reached"); at 32768
it ran free until the harness killed the run. THE CONTEXT AND THE REASONING
CAP HAVE TO MOVE TOGETHER -- fixing one alone just changes the symptom.

MEASURED AGAINST THE LIVE DAEMON, same prompt:
    default (no cap)          hangs > 720s
    max_tokens=800             4s, 78 completion tokens, correct JSON
    reasoning_effort="none"    1s, 19 completion tokens, correct JSON
Verified end to end through langchain after the patch: 1.2s round trip,
content='{"ok":true}', 6 output tokens.

