  vsc-mcp's "Access denied" is worth a second look: the server confines file
  access to a workspace root and refused a path outside it. That is a security
  property being ENFORCED, i.e. a true negative, and it is exactly the class of
  property (a path confined to a declared workspace) that HANDOFF section 10
  argues is inside ToFu's reach and outside a taint formulation. Consider
  pointing it at its own workspace so the boundary can actually be probed.

