*** READ THIS BEFORE USING "240 CONFIGS" ***
The survey tests ONE representative tool per repo. 240 is therefore an UPPER
BOUND that assumes every tool in a repo behaves like its representative, which
is false: google-workspace was 3/33 and gmail-mcp 2/5 on their representative,
and most of their remaining tools need OAuth. The only authority on a given
tool is that tool's own EXEC_SUMMARY from a real run. Do not put 240 in the
paper as "tools fuzzed".

