  Both are LOCAL tools -- no credential wall, and the introspection oracle can
  observe them IF they are Python. Check: both are node, so the JS
  instrumentation gap (open mismatch 3) still applies to their file operations.

================================================================
HOSTED ARM: gpt-4.1 -- FIRST RUN, 2026-09-10 16:14-16:48, 9 configs, 0.56h
================================================================

SETUP (eval/run_arm_gpt41.sh)
  gpt-4.1 at https://api.openai.com/v1, temperature=0, seed=20260910.
  CHOSEN OVER gpt-5 / o3 / o4-mini DELIBERATELY: those are reasoning models,
  they ignore `temperature` and reject max_tokens ("Unsupported parameter:
  'max_tokens' is not supported with this model. Use 'max_completion_tokens'").
  The gemma4 arm runs at temperature=0 with reasoning DISABLED so that the model
  is the only variable; pairing it with a model that reasons unconditionally
  would confound the comparison. gpt-5 belongs in the thinking arm (item 24).
  gpt-4.1 also REJECTS reasoning_effort outright -- 400 "Unrecognized request
  argument supplied" -- and that 400 arrives at INVOKE time, so it would have
  killed every call of a campaign. llm.py now drops the argument and rebuilds
  the client on that specific error.

RESULT SEPARATION (--arm / TOFU_ARM)
  eval/state/runs.<arm>.jsonl, eval/runs/<arm>/, eval/corpora_<arm>/,
  eval/metrics_<arm>/. Without it done_set() would make the second arm SKIP
  every config the first arm ran, and summarize() would average two models
  together. Default ("" ) keeps the existing layout byte-for-byte.

*** THE NUMBER THAT MATTERS: 9/9 EXECUTABLE, 9/9 llm_selection ok,
*** 9/9 llm_seeds ok, 0 harness errors.
  First arm where every run reached the target AND the LLM stage worked on
  every config. gemma4's comparable figures across 77 runs: selection ok on 31,
  executability yes on 7.
  LLM TAX: gpt-4.1 ~8s per config (select 4.0s + seedgen 3.6s) vs gemma4 ~270s.
  ~35x. That tax was ~60% of every gemma4 run, so the hosted arm is roughly
  2.3x faster end to end at the same 180s budget.

ALL 761 ALERTS TRIAGED -> FALSE POSITIVE OR KNOWN NOISE. 4 signatures:

  check_path_traversal   426 alerts  bhouston/mcp-server-text-editor
      The tool REFUSED every one, in a normal MCP result:
        {"success":false,"message":"Path must be absolute"}
        {"success":false,"message":"File not found: /etc/passwd..."}
        {"success":false,"message":"new_str parameter is required..."}
      No isError, no top-level error -- a STRUCTURED refusal inside
      content[].text. BUG 18, the same failure as bug 17 one layer deeper.
      FIXED: _inband_error parses a content block's JSON and treats an explicit
      "success": false (or its own error) as a failed execution. Prose is still
      not guessed at -- "an error occurred" does not count.

  check_invalid_json     313 alerts  sequential-thinking
      NOT a tool defect. A SELECTION error, and a usable RQ2 datum: gpt-4.1
      chose check_invalid_json for `thought`, a FREE-TEXT field. The sanitizer
      fires whenever mutated text contains "{" and does not parse, which for
      free text is meaningless. Report as selection precision.
      NOTE the frontier model made a selection error of the same KIND as
      llama3.1:8b's markitdown-for-appium -- applying a format checker to a
      field whose contract does not mention that format. Worth saying in RQ2:
      the failure mode is not exclusive to small models.

  check_process_and_fd_leaks  4 tools   -- item 40, UNFIXED
  check_resource_exhaustion   4 tools   -- item 39, UNFIXED
      "Execution took 5.01 seconds (Limit: 2.0s)" on tools calling the National
      Park Service API over HTTPS. A 5s network fetch is normal.

QUARANTINED: eval/state/quarantine-fp-gpt41-20260910/ (6 records + logs +
WHY.md). Active gpt41 index is 3 runs, 0 alerts.

- TO DOUBLE-CHECK (Ananto, do not erase until confirmed done):
   45. sec10_ethical.tex STILL OWES the hosted-model note. This arm sends
