*** THE BLOCKER: 0 PYTHON TARGETS HAVE EVER BEEN PREPARED. ***
    prepared repos: 33  -- ALL 33 ARE NODE
    configs:       470  -- ALL 470 ARE NODE
    python repos attempted: 75.  python repos prepared: 0.  100% failure.
  Failure reasons:
    23  "No module named <pkg>" when launched
    18  pip -r requirements.txt failed
    14  pip install -e . failed
    11  no python entrypoint
     9  no tools/list reply

  ROOT CAUSE, read from eval/prepare_targets.py: sys.executable is used for
  BOTH installing a target and launching it --
      :81  run([sys.executable, "-m", "pip", "install", "-q", "-r", "requirements.txt"])
      :86  run([sys.executable, "-m", "pip", "install", "-q", "-e", "."])
      :136 return sys.executable, [fp]
      :147 return sys.executable, ["-m", mod]
  So every Python target's dependencies are installed into ToFu's OWN venv,
  where they collide with each other and with ToFu's pins (mcp==2.2.0, atheris,
  langchain-*). Several failures are literally the mcp<2 migration error. The
  "No module named" bucket is repos that ship only requirements.txt: their deps
  install but the package itself never does, so `python -m <mod>` cannot resolve.
  HANDOFF already gives the Cisco scanner its own venv for exactly this reason
  ("installing it into the toolfuzzer venv would change the versions the ToFu
  campaign runs under"). That was never applied to targets.

  *** WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN ANYTHING ELSE OPEN ***
  The introspection oracle -- Table 3's 21 tracers, all 19 of the runner-fed
  oracle inputs, sec4.5.1, RQ3 -- WORKS ONLY ON PYTHON. Node gets coverage and
  nothing else. So ToFu has never once run its own oracle on a real corpus
  target. Every campaign to date has been the one language where the central
  mechanism is switched off. Fixing preparation to give each target its own
  venv converts 0 python targets into potentially dozens and is the
  precondition for ANY finding the paper can claim.

