================================================================
2026-09-11  SINK-PROBE PROVENANCE + A CORRECTION I OWE
================================================================
WHERE THE 21 FAMILIES CAME FROM: they are the inverse image of ToFu's own
oracle, not a taxonomy. extract_tools.py:38 says so -- "sink patterns, keyed
to ToFu's 21 introspection tracers". Verified 1:1 against
src/sanitizers/introspection.py: 21 *Tracer classes, 21 SINKS keys, names
match exactly (only SSLCertificateValidationTracer -> SSLCertValidation).
Consequence: the table cannot be captioned "sink prevalence in MCP servers"
without being circular. Captioned as TRACER COVERAGE instead.

CORRECTION (mine, stated twice to Ananto before being caught). I claimed
UnrestrictedIPBinding's pattern was "server|port|host". WRONG. Two different
proxies exist in this project and I conflated them:
  (a) nazmul.todo:480 -- keyword proxy over repo name/title/description.
      IPBinding 84.7%. THAT one is the "server|port|host" probe.
  (b) extract_tools.py SINKS -- static scan of cloned source. IPBinding
      26.0% py / 37.1% node. Pattern is r'0\.0\.0\.0', r'host\s*=\s*["\']0',
      r'listen\s*\('.
The table's numbers come from (b). Still over-broad -- r'listen\s*\(' matches
every socket/HTTP server -- but the REASON I gave was wrong. Footnote in
tab_corpus.tex corrected.

NINE LOW-SPECIFICITY PROBES (match language constructs, not sink APIs):
  LogInjection (print(), SensitiveDataLogging (os.environ -- no logging at all
  despite the name), FileAccess (any open(), FileWrite (any .write(),
  ReDoS (any re.compile), BlockingEventLoopCall (any sleep/sync IO, and it
  SHARES readFileSync with FileAccess and execSync with CommandExecution ->
  probes are NOT disjoint, marginals cannot be summed), LoopCondition
  (while True), UnrestrictedIPBinding, WeakPRNG (random.shuffle counts).
  These 9 are valid as an UPPER BOUND on tracer reach. They are NOT valid for
  stratification, prevalence ranking, or as detection-rate denominators.
TWELVE SPECIFIC PROBES report 2-5% and are informative (Deserialization,
  SSLCertValidation, XXE, NonceReuse, WeakHash, ...).

NOT MEASURED: no hand-labelled sample, so no precision/recall, no error bar.
Also cannot decompose which subpattern drove a family hit -- results.jsonl
stores only the per-family total. Would need a rescan.

