ITEM 51 -- PER-TARGET VENV. DONE. eval/prepare_targets.py.
  Before: 0 of 75 Python repos prepared. After: 6 of 21 Set A Python repos
  READY, 60 Python configs written. FIRST PYTHON TARGETS ToFu HAS EVER HAD.
  Three distinct root causes, all measured, none guessed:
   (a) sys.executable everywhere -- deps installed into ToFu's OWN venv and
       collided with our pins (mcp==2.2.0). Even the one correct path,
       `uv sync --frozen`, built dest/.venv and then LAUNCHED WITH
       sys.executable anyway, throwing the good venv away.
   (b) uv venv defaults to the newest Python present (3.14.4 here). Mid-2025
       deps (pydantic-core 2.27) ship no 3.14 wheels -> source build -> needs
       Rust -> fail. Pinned TARGET_PYTHON=3.11 (env TOFU_TARGET_PYTHON).
   (c) Repos pin their code but NOT their SDK. mindmap-mcp-server asks for
       "mcp>=1.2.0" -> resolves to mcp 2.x -> FastMCP renamed to MCPServer ->
       dies on import. Now resolving with `uv --exclude-newer <last_commit>`,
       which is both contemporary AND reproducible. Falls back to an unpinned
       retry (noted as "no-cutoff") because some repos were updated after the
       snapshot and genuinely need 2.x.
  Also: target_env() strips VIRTUAL_ENV/PYTHONPATH/PYTHONHOME/CONDA_PREFIX from
  child processes, and detect_launch() now prefers the venv's CONSOLE SCRIPT
  over `-m pkg` (a "pkg:main" entry point is a FUNCTION; `-m pkg` fails with
  "cannot be directly executed" unless __main__.py exists -- that was 2 of 10).
  New flags: --only-lang {python,node}, --retry-skipped (item 52 needs it).

REMAINING PYTHON SKIPS (15 of 21), now with HONEST reasons:
  genuinely not our fault: repo SyntaxError (VibeCheck), missing credentials
