*** BUG 20 -- INSTRUMENT REPORTED ITSELF AS A FINDING (found live) ***
  During the gpt41-full run Ananto saw HIT [1..4/470] on mcp-appium-gestures,
  alerts=1,5,3,21, sigs=1. All 21 on generate-swipe-code were:
    "Resource exhaustion/Timeout detected: Execution took 5.01s (Limit: 2.0s)"
    "Tool Output : None"
    "[JSRunner] Socket Communication Error: timed out"
  js_runner.py:166 sets sock.settimeout(5.0); config.timeout_limit is 2.0.
  A TIMED-OUT READ THEREFORE ALWAYS EXCEEDS THE THRESHOLD. Nothing executed --
  output is None -- yet it scored as resource exhaustion. The runner then
  restarts the server, whose boot time makes the next read time out too, so one
  dead server cascades into many identical "findings".
  FIX: _check_resource_exhaustion(elapsed, res) now returns False when res
  indicates a transport failure. 6 regression tests, fixtures verbatim from
  eval/runs/gpt41-full/...generate-swipe-code.log.
  HONEST LIMITATION, stated in the docstring: a GENUINE hang also surfaces as a
  socket timeout, so this trades recall for soundness. Telling "tool hung" from
  "server died" needs a liveness probe after the timeout -- item 39, open.
  Run was killed at 4/470 and must be restarted. Nothing from it is evidence.

  Also fixed: test_no_undefined_names_anywhere now ignores eval/targets/,
  which since item 51 contains third-party site-packages. run_eval.py's
  preflight checks 4 explicit files, so it was never affected.

