Ananto asked for all 8 logs to be checked rather than the 4 I had seen. Right
call -- they were NOT all the same failure. 56 alerts total, TWO classes.

CLASS 1 -- 42 alerts, check_resource_exhaustion. ALL transport failures.
  42 exhaustion alerts vs 43 socket timeouts in the same logs; every elapsed in
  [5.00, 5.17] against a 5.0s sock.settimeout and a 2.0s threshold; every one
  with "Tool Output : None". Bug 20, already fixed. Not evidence.

CLASS 2 -- 14 alerts, check_path_traversal, ArchimedesCrypto/excel-reader-mcp
  ::export_to_json. "Silent Bug Alert: sanitizers flagged this input as
  malicious, but the tool executed successfully." DIFFERENT MECHANISM, and it
  led to a second, worse bug.

*** BUG 21 -- TARGETS RAN FROM ToFu'S REPO ROOT, NOT THEIR OWN DIRECTORY ***
  prepare_targets.py has ALWAYS written "cwd" into every config. NOTHING EVER
  READ IT. js_runner.py called subprocess.Popen(cmd, ...) with no cwd=, so the
  target inherited ToFu's cwd. src/__main__.py never parsed the key, and
  FuzzerConfig had no field for it.
  REPRODUCED BOTH WAYS, same input, outputPath="../../../../tmp/evil.json":
    cwd = target's own dir -> MCP error -32603 ENOENT. Tool fails safely.
    cwd = ToFu repo root   -> SUCCESS, wrote /tmp/evil.json (content [] then
                              [{"col":"val"}]). Four levels up from the repo
                              root is exactly "/", which is why the escape
                              landed in /tmp and not where cwd arithmetic on
                              the target dir predicted.
  The two files found on disk (/tmp/evil.json, /tmp/evil.jso, 2 bytes each,
  mtimes 02:14:56 and 02:16:33, inside the run window) are preserved under the
  session scratchpad evidence/ dir.
  COMPOUNDING: fuzzer.py's traversal oracle resolved allowed_dir as
  "allowed_workspace_dir or os.getcwd()" -- so escapes were judged against
  ToFu's OWN tree. Two independent expressions of the same confusion.
  FIX: FuzzerConfig.target_cwd; __main__ reads config["cwd"] and also seeds
  allowed_workspace_dir from it; JSRunner takes cwd= and passes it to Popen;
  fuzzer passes config.target_cwd when constructing JSRunner; allowed_dir now
  prefers target_cwd and keeps os.getcwd() only as a last resort.
  6 regression tests, including one asserting EVERY prepared config has a cwd.

  VERDICT ON THE 14 ALERTS: NOT SOUND EVIDENCE AS RECORDED. Under the correct
  cwd the same input fails with ENOENT, so the observed escape to /tmp is our
  artefact. DO NOT report them. But do NOT dismiss the underlying question
  either: export_to_json performs no validation of outputPath, so "../evil.json"
  would still escape into eval/targets/ under a correct cwd. Whether that is a
  real finding must be RE-TESTED after bug 21, not inferred from these logs.
   54. RE-TEST excel-reader-mcp::export_to_json outputPath validation under the
       corrected cwd before writing anything about it.

  WIDER IMPACT, not yet quantified: every Node target so far ran from the wrong
  directory. Any target that reads relative config/data files was mis-run, and
  some "no tools/list reply" and executability failures may be this. The
  15-executable / 18-not-executable split predates the fix and is now suspect.
