CONFIRMED
 V1  ArchimedesCrypto/excel-reader-mcp  export_to_json + export_to_csv
     ARBITRARY FILE WRITE via outputPath (CWE-73).  Only check is
     typeof outputPath === 'string' (export-to-json.ts:15, :89 writeFileSync;
     export-to-csv.ts:100).  Reproduced UNDER THE CORRECT cwd (item 54):
       absolute path outside cwd -> SUCCESS, file written
       "../../x.json" relative   -> SUCCESS, wrote eval/x.json
     Content = xlsx cell values -> attacker controls content AND location.
     Same class as Pierre's "insufficiently constrained output path".
     Schema text: "Path to save CSV file (optional...)" -- no scoping promise,
     so a reviewer can call it intended. Argue from the paper's threat model.
     DETECTION HONESTY: ToFu found it ONCE, in the quarantined bug-21 run
     (wrote /tmp/evil.json). Under the fixed harness, 180s, outputPath was
     mutated to only '' and the literal seed placeholder (the tool duly wrote
     "predefined_seed:output.json" inside its cwd). Never an escaping path.
     -> item 48 (mutation) is why the fixed fuzzer did not re-find it.
 V2  Heratiki/locallama-mcp  subtask_results.log
     LOG INJECTION + UNBOUNDED LOG (CWE-117, CWE-779).  codeTaskCoordinator.ts
     logSubtaskResult() appends `## Subtask: ${subtask.description}` and a
     ```-fenced ${result} RAW via appendFileSync, no sanitising, no cap (file
     only reset at startup, :39). description = the LLM-supplied task text.
     ON DISK after ~1.4h: 602 KB, 644 lines containing NUL, 6 headings split
     by injected control chars (\x13 \x0b \x10) so the record structure is
     broken; e.g. heading '## Subtask: "task": "Read file ../../../../etc/
     passwd..."' followed by a raw '\x0b\x10ut_length": 50...' line.
     0 ANSI CSI sequences -> terminal-escape angle is weak; stick to CWE-117.
     ToFu's check_log_injection flagged 43 inputs on preemptive_route_task and
     5 on rate_model; routing/index.ts:1046-1094 is the path from that tool
     into codeTaskCoordinator, so the fuzzer flagged the right input class on
     the right tool. The SINK itself was confirmed by hand (JS -> no tracer).
 V3  Heratiki/locallama-mcp  update_server
     INPUT-INDEPENDENT: zero-arg, zero-auth tool runs
       git pull origin future-testing && npm install && npm run build
     (updater/index.ts:110-117, execFile, no guard) and the server respawns on
     the new build. Any MCP client can make the server fetch+execute a
     hardcoded DEV branch. Pierre's "input-independent" class.
     CAVEAT: `future-testing` DOES NOT EXIST on origin (only main). The tool is
     currently inert -- git pull fails after ~2s, which is exactly the 3
     "2.12/2.64/3.15s" exhaustion alerts (genuine slow-but-completed calls; the
     bug-20 guard correctly let them through). Target stayed at the pinned
     commit, node_modules untouched. Latent, not live.

NOT FINDINGS (checked, with reasons)
  - 42 exhaustion alerts = socket timeouts (bug 20).  7 path_traversal on
