  google-workspace 5561 -- POSITIVE CONTROL. manage_scratchpad got 208
                       check_path_traversal yet is SAFE: resolveWorkspacePath()
                       sanitises+resolves+rejects escapes (workspace.ts:161),
                       verifyPathSafety() adds realpath symlink check. This is
                       exactly what excel-reader OMITS. USE AS CONTRAST PAIR IN
                       THE PAPER: same alert, opposite verdict, decided by
                       reading the sink -- the core triage argument.
  apisix 3          -- temp_file_leak on error path; n_exec=2000 n_success=0
                       (no APISIX backend, ECONN). Environment exclusion.
  pluggedin 1       -- invalid_json; tool needs API key, never executed. Excl.

ROOT CAUSE OF THE FP CASCADES (extends bug 22): check_url_structure_and_parsing,
  check_url_hostname_canonicalization, check_url_ssrf_ip_ranges, and
  check_strict_har_security_contract / check_strict_markitdown_security_contract
  are NOT in the fuzzer.py:944 parameter-name context guard, so they run on
  every string argument and on every tool regardless of relevance. Item 56 must
  cover ALL of these, not only check_path_traversal.
   56. (EXPANDED) Context-guard the full string-sanitizer set, not just
       path_traversal: add url-family (needs url/uri/link/endpoint/host name
       match) and scope the *_security_contract sanitizers to their own tool
       families (har -> har tools, markitdown -> markitdown tools). Until then
       every silent-bug count on a non-matching arg is noise.

TRIAGE PRINCIPLE CONFIRMED (item 60): raw hit count is anti-correlated with
  real bugs here. The two confirmed findings came from 7 and ~1800 hits; the
  10040-hit repo was pure FP. Rank leads by SINK, not by alert volume.

