2026-09-11  CISCO MCP SCANNER: NEVER RAN BEFORE -> NOW WORKS. 3 BUGS FIXED.
================================================================
Ananto asked: did we run Cisco MCP Scanner? Answer: NO -- two prior attempts
(appium, excel-reader) both crashed and produced zero results. Now fixed and
producing honest output.

THREE INDEPENDENT BLOCKERS, all fixed:
  1. THEIR BUG. Benchmarks/Cisco-MCP-Scanner/mcpscanner/cli.py had a local
     `import os` at line 2377 inside async def main() (spans 1024..2377). Python
     function-scope rule makes `os` local for the WHOLE function, so the earlier
     os.environ[...] at line 1680 raised
       UnboundLocalError: cannot access local variable 'os'
     -> EVERY stdio scan crashed before starting. FIX: removed the redundant
     local import (module already imports os at line 32). Patch is marked
     "PATCH (ToFu)" in their cli.py. DISCLOSE/RECORD: we patched the baseline
     tool to run it; state this in the paper's baseline methodology.
  2. OUR STALE VENV. The scanner venv was built when the repo lived at
     /pseclab/toolfuzzer/; after the move to /pseclab/ToFu/ the console-script
     shims still had `#!/.../toolfuzzer/.venv/bin/python` (venvs are not
     relocatable) -> FileNotFoundError: .venv/bin/mcp-scanner. FIX: `uv sync`
     in the scanner dir rebuilt shims at the current path. The os-patch
     survives because install is editable.
  3. OUR RUNNER (eval/run_cisco_scanner.py), two bugs:
     (a) It read a --output .json file, but `--format raw` prints the report to
         STDOUT and writes no file -> json.load failed, reported as a fake
         per-repo error. FIX: parse stdout when the --output file is absent,
         persisting it to the .json for inspection.
     (b) count_findings phantom-counted: line was
           c = int(val.get("total_findings") or 0) or (1 if val else 0)
         A SAFE tool reports total_findings=0 with a populated result dict, so
         the fallback counted it as 1 -> excel-reader showed 14 "findings" when
         the raw verdict is 14x severity=SAFE, is_safe=True, total_findings=0.
         FIX: total_findings is authoritative when present; the truthy fallback
         fires only when the count key is ABSENT and severity is not SAFE.
         THIS IS THE SAME PHANTOM-FINDING FAMILY AS THE TOFU INSTRUMENT BUGS --
         an unverified count is exactly what CLAUDE.md forbids. Caught by
         cross-checking the printed count against the raw scanner JSON.

VERIFIED yara-only smoke (2 servers): 19 tools scanned, 0 flagged, 0 findings,
  matching the raw JSON. Scanner sees 41 ready servers / 537 tools from
  eval/state/prepared.jsonl. Stale pre-fix state quarantined under
  eval/state/quarantine-cisco-stale-toolfuzzer-path/.

HOW TO RUN (for Ananto's terminal):
  yara-only, all servers, no LLM needed:
    .venv/bin/python eval/run_cisco_scanner.py --analyzers yara
  yara + LLM (llm analyzer): default model is llama3.1:8b which we DROPPED and
  ollama was not running. Point it at a live model first, e.g.
    CISCO_LLM_MODEL=ollama_chat/gemma4:12b  (start ollama), or a gpt-4.1 LiteLLM
    id with the OpenAI key. Then add llm to --analyzers.
  The `api` analyzer needs a paid Cisco AI Defense subscription -> DISABLED.
  Baseline is open-source analyzers only; state as a limitation (Table 2).
