2026-09-11  VIPER-MCP: PHASE II IS HOLLOW WITHOUT CODEQL, AND THE ARTIFACT
            NEVER INSTRUMENTS NODE. Three patches applied, all marked.
================================================================
Empirical run (excel-reader, --skip-codeql, rounds=2): "Fuzzing completed.
Anomalies: 5" -- but every anomaly was tool_error, oracle.json was 0 bytes,
and static_context.json held ONE placeholder entry
  tool_name="mcp_tool", vulnerability_type="general", tool_candidates=[]
so the agent literally called search_text(filePath="mcp_tool.xlsx"). Without
SARIF there is no target list: --skip-codeql fuzzes a synthetic target.
=> CODEQL IS NOT OPTIONAL FOR VIPER. "Phase II now, Phase I later" is wrong.
   Any Viper number requires `brew install codeql` (2.27.0 >= 2.16) first.

FIVE ERROR KINDS IN THE LOG, THREE CAUSES:
 (1) base_url: "" -- src/llm/__init__.py:10 hands cfg["base_url"] straight to
     AsyncOpenAI(base_url=...); the SDK treats "" as a literal URL ->
     "Connection error" for seed_generator, mutator, strategy scoring AND
     hit_judge (which inherits prompt_llm at engine.py:326). The langchain
     agent tolerates "", which is exactly why --test-agent passed while fuzz
     failed. Their shipped config.yaml has base_url: "" too -> their default
     is broken for OpenAI. FIX (wrapper): omit the key unless OPENAI_BASE_URL
     is set; set llm.hit_judge explicitly (it is read by config.py:60 but
     absent from the shipped yaml).
 (2) name 'prompts' is not defined -- src/feedback/optimizer.py:78 uses
     prompts.SCHEDULING_PROMPT (defined in src/fuzz/prompts.py) without
     importing it. THEIR BUG, masked until the LLM works. PATCH (ToFu):
     `from ..fuzz import prompts`.
 (3) NO NODE INSTRUMENTATION. src/utils/instrumentation.py has ONLY
     inject_python_hook_env (PYTHONPATH/.pth). instrumentation/javascript/
     node_hook.js exists -- hooks fs.writeFile*/appendFile*/child_process.exec
     and logs to $MCP_FUZZER_ORACLE_LOG -- but nothing ever adds
     NODE_OPTIONS=--require for it. On every Node target the runtime oracle
     is blind: no hook_init, no sink events. Viper AS SHIPPED could not have
     observed V1's writeFileSync regardless of its LLM or CodeQL output.
     PATCH (ToFu): inject_node_hook_env() mirroring the python one, wired in
     surrogate_agent.py next to it. Their hook file, their env var; we added
     the one line that loads it. STATE THIS IN METHODOLOGY exactly as we
     state the Cisco `os` patch.
 (4) error='target_call_chain' (KeyError in _score_round_with_llm) -- likely
     downstream of (1) (fallback dict lacking the key); falls back to
     rule-based scoring (strategy.py:158). Re-check after (1).
 (5) per-target oracle: node_hook default is <viper>/results/oracle.json,
     SHARED across a loop. Wrapper now sets output.oracle_path and
     MCP_FUZZER_ORACLE_LOG per target and records hook_injected /
     n_oracle_events so a blind run is visible in the index.

WRAPPER (eval/run_viper.py) now: all three LLM roles explicit, base_url
omitted, per-target oracle, recursive fuzz_results scan, n_anomalies,
hook_injected flag. Re-smoke pending.
   69. brew install codeql (user). Until then no Viper number is valid.
   70. Viper deviations to state: gpt-4.1 (theirs gpt-5.4), temperature 0
       (theirs 0.7), three patches (base_url handling is config not code;
       prompts import; node hook injection), CodeQL 2.27.0.

VIPER RE-SMOKE AFTER PATCHES (excel-reader, rounds=2, --skip-codeql, 29.3s):
  VERIFIED FIXED: zero "Connection error" (base_url omitted -> seed_generator,
    hit_judge, mutator all reach gpt-4.1); zero NameError (prompts import).
    Agent now discovers and targets a REAL tool: "Discovery threshold met via
    template=minimal_embedding target=read_excel"; interactions show real
    read_excel / list_sheets calls.
  STILL OPEN:
   (i) hook_injected=False, oracle.json EMPTY -> my NODE_OPTIONS injection did
       not take effect in the child. Diagnosing: hook-works-by-hand vs env
       not propagated through langchain-mcp-adapters stdio config.
  (ii) "LLM round scoring failed target=read_excel -> none_detected
       error='target_call_chain'" x8 -> KeyError, NOT a connection error now.
       Suspect prompts.ROUND_SCORING_TEMPLATE uses NAMED {target_call_chain}
       placeholders while strategy.py calls .format(positional...). Their bug;
       degrades the LLM feedback loop to rule-based scoring (graceful, but it
       IS the core of Phase II). Checking placeholders before patching.
  (iii) "No target call chains from CodeQL; using single generic target." ->
       confirms Phase II is untargeted without SARIF, BUT the agent still
       self-discovers tools from tools/list and probes them with
       vulnerability_type=none_detected. So skip-codeql = generic probing,
       not zero. Still not a Viper result.
  (iv) 6 anomalies, ALL tool_error "File not found": the agent guesses
       filenames; there is no seed file. excel-reader's export_to_json reads
       the xlsx BEFORE writeFileSync, so with no real input file Viper can
       NEVER reach V1's write sink -- the exact problem ToFu's file-backed
       parameters (predefined_seed:*.xlsx) solved (nazmul.todo 2026-09-10).
       COMPARISON POINT: file-taking tools are structurally out of Viper's
       reach without a fixture mechanism it does not have.

VIPER HARNESS: RESOLVED (excel-reader, rounds=2, --skip-codeql, 37.6s)
  All three PATCH (ToFu) edits verified in a live run:
   - base_url omitted            -> 0 "Connection error"
   - prompts import              -> 0 NameError
   - keyword .format (strategy.py ROUND_SCORING_TEMPLATE, optimizer.py
     SCHEDULING_PROMPT; both templates use NAMED fields, both call sites were
     positional) -> 0 "LLM round scoring failed", 0 "Mutator choice failed".
     The LLM feedback loop -- the core of their Phase II -- now actually runs.
   - node hook injection (inject_node_hook_env) -> hook_injected=True; a
     hook_init event carrying the child's pid/cwd landed in the per-target
     oracle.json (same signature as the hand-injected control).
  Probe of the real builder (src.agent.create_agent_from_config) shows the
  stdio env handed to langchain-mcp-adapters = {MCP_FUZZER_ORACLE_LOG,
  NODE_OPTIONS=--require .../node_hook.js}; the adapter only expands ${VAR};
  the mcp SDK MERGES with get_default_environment() (mcp/client/stdio.py:126).
  Earlier "hook_injected=False" was a MEASUREMENT artefact: RuntimeMonitor
  consume-and-clears oracle.json between rounds, so the file left on disk
  under-reports. Wrapper now derives hook_injected / max_oracle_hits_in_round
  from fuzzer.log as well ("oracle_hits=N" per hit_judge line).
  Behaviour observed = as designed: agent generated "Read the Excel file
  located at ../../etc/passwd" -> read_excel -> "File not found". Viper does
  taint-style traversal probing on the READ side.
  max_oracle_hits=0, export_to_json NEVER CALLED in 2 rounds -> V1 not reached;
  and it cannot be reached without a real xlsx fixture (read precedes write).
  Their default provider path is probably deepseek (the only branch tolerant
  of base_url ""), which explains why the openai path shipped untested.
  STILL REQUIRED FOR ANY VIPER NUMBER: CodeQL (brew install codeql, 2.27.0).
  "No target call chains from CodeQL; using single generic target." on every
  skip-codeql run. Harness is ready the moment codeql is on PATH.

