================================================================
2026-09-12  SANDBOX: why targets must not run on the host, + the Docker plan
================================================================
Ananto asked why the servers run on his machine and not a sandbox. Correct
instinct. Verified exposure, NOT hypothetical:
  1. npm install runs WITHOUT --ignore-scripts (prepare_targets.py:188) ->
     an untrusted package's postinstall executes as the user AT PREPARE TIME,
     before any fuzzing. pip sdists (setup.py) same.
  2. A target ALREADY wrote to the real FS this session: bug-21 residue
     (findings/evidence/bug21-repo-root-writes/: output.json, C:\temp\out.json,
     earlier /tmp/evil.json). Benign tool, but proves reach; a malicious one
     writing ~/.ssh/authorized_keys looks identical to the harness.
  3. Prepared OS/command tools: DesktopCommanderMCP (26, "OS & Terminal
     Control"), mcpFirebird (SQL), apisix. Viper feeds them ../../etc/passwd
     and command-injection payloads by design -- at the host.
  No sandbox existed: targets ran as the user, unconfined. Not a decision,
  just how the harness was built.

DECISION (Ananto): Docker container.

DESIGN (files written, build pending Docker daemon):
  Dockerfile.sandbox  python3.11-slim + node22 + clang/llvm (atheris builds
                      libFuzzer from source on Linux) + uv; builds ToFu's OWN
                      Linux venv (/opt/tofu-venv) from requirements.txt; runs
                      as non-root uid 1000, no host home.
  .dockerignore       keeps the 7.1GB eval/targets and all venvs OUT of the
                      build context.
  eval/sandbox.sh     build | shell | prepare | run | smoke. Mounts the repo
                      at its IDENTICAL host path (so prepared.jsonl absolute
                      paths stay valid; an escape lands in the container, not
                      $HOME). Repo mounted READ-ONLY; writable overlays only at
                      eval/{targets,state,runs,metrics,corpora,configs} backed
                      by eval/sandbox/* so the LIVE host campaign is untouched.
                      --memory 8g --cpus 4 --pids-limit 1024; egress ON (LLM +
                      git clone); .env mounted ro, OPENAI_API_KEY passed by -e.

  Why whole-harness-in-container: python_runner imports the target in-process
  to hook builtins.open, so fuzzer+target share a process -> same container.

STATUS / RISKS TO RESOLVE ON BUILD (cannot verify until daemon is up):
  - atheris==3.0.0 on arm64 Linux may need the exact libFuzzer archive name;
    the Dockerfile probes clang -print-file-name but expect 1-2 build iters.
  - node-gyp native deps in some targets need python3+make (present) but may
    still fail per-repo (that is a target property, record as a skip).
  - macOS .venv / Cisco / Viper venvs are NOT reused (Linux). v1 sandboxes the
    TOFU fuzzer (the core, and what actually executes targets adversarially).
    Cisco already ran (metadata-only, does not execute tools). MCPSafety/Viper
    launch servers too -> sandbox them next (v2) before their final numbers.
  - Existing gpt41-full + cisco results were produced ON THE HOST. Findings
    (V1/V2) stand regardless, but the PUBLISHED numbers should be reproduced
    in-container. Flag in methodology.
   71. Start Docker Desktop; ./eval/sandbox.sh build; ./eval/sandbox.sh smoke.
       Iterate the Dockerfile on atheris if needed.
   72. After the host gpt41-full run finishes: re-prepare + re-run in-sandbox
       (eval/sandbox/), compare to host results, adopt the sandbox numbers.
   73. v2: sandbox the baselines (MCPSafety, Viper) the same way before their
       numbers are published.

