2026-09-12  HOST CAMPAIGN STOPPED; CAMPAIGN CONTINUES IN THE SANDBOX
================================================================
Ananto stopped the host gpt41-full run (see count below) and confirmed the
architecture: ToFu's introspectors hook the target IN-PROCESS, so fuzzer and
target live in the same container -- whole harness in Docker (Option B). The
"ToFu on host, server in Docker" split was rejected on two hard facts:
python_runner imports the target in-process (oracle dies across a boundary),
and js_runner talks over a /tmp Unix socket with the coverage wrapper inside
the node process. The log-writing concern is moot: bind mounts write straight
to the host FS in real time.

ARM NAMING: sandbox runs use --arm gpt41-sandbox (index
eval/sandbox/state/runs.gpt41-sandbox.jsonl). Host arm gpt41-full is frozen as
host-run evidence. NEVER merge the two indices; published numbers = sandbox.

FIRST BUILD FAILED on atheris: my Dockerfile used
  LIBFUZZER_LIB=$(clang -print-file-name=... || echo "")
but -print-file-name NEVER fails -- it echoes the bare name back when the
file is missing -- so the fallback never fired and atheris got a relative
filename. Probe container showed the archive IS present after `apt-get
install clang llvm`: /usr/lib/llvm-14/lib/clang/14.0.6/lib/linux/
libclang_rt.fuzzer_no_main-aarch64.a (Debian clang 14.0.6). Dockerfile now
resolves it in its own RUN, asserts an absolute existing path (fail-loud),
adds procps+lsof (python:3.11-slim ships no `ps`; _ps_snapshot would fail
closed = no process-leak detection), and self-tests `import atheris, mcp`.
A background probe is compiling atheris with LIBFUZZER_LIB set to confirm.

NEW: eval/run_sandbox_campaign.sh  prepare|run|status  (wraps sandbox.sh;
TOFU_PY=/opt/tofu-venv/bin/python; ARM=gpt41-sandbox). run_arm_gpt41.sh and
run_overnight.sh now honour TOFU_PY.
NEXT: confirm atheris probe -> docker build -> sandbox.sh smoke -> re-prepare
all sets in-sandbox (npm/pip postinstall now confined) -> run.

ATHERIS-IN-LINUX PROBE: CONFIRMED. In python:3.11-slim-bookworm + `apt-get
install clang llvm build-essential python3-dev`, with
  LIBFUZZER_LIB=/usr/lib/llvm-14/lib/clang/14.0.6/lib/linux/libclang_rt.fuzzer_no_main-aarch64.a
`uv pip install atheris==3.0.0` builds in 1m04s and `import atheris` succeeds.
So the whole-harness-in-container design is viable; the split is not needed.
Image build (fixed Dockerfile) running in background -> eval/sandbox/build.log.
Host gpt41-full frozen at 423/530 (last write 2026-09-12 00:51:29).

SANDBOX WRITE-PATH AUDIT: repo is mounted READ-ONLY, so every dir the harness
writes must be an overlay or a run dies with EROFS halfway. Overlays now:
targets state runs configs seeds metrics corpora metrics_$ARM corpora_$ARM,
plus a private tmpfs on /tmp (js_runner's Unix socket + target scratch; never
the host /tmp). ARM passed into the container (ARM, TOFU_ARM) so arm-scoped
dirs line up with the overlays. Any new eval/* write path added to the harness
must be added to OVERLAYS in eval/sandbox.sh -- noted in the script header.

SANDBOX BUILD #2 FAILED -- and the fail-loud check I added did its job:
  FATAL: libFuzzer archive not found (got: libclang_rt.fuzzer_no_main-aarch64.a)
ROOT CAUSE: the archive ships in libclang-rt-14-dev, which is only a
RECOMMENDED dependency of clang. The Dockerfile installs with
--no-install-recommends (good hygiene) so apt silently dropped it; the probe
container used plain apt-get (recommends on) and therefore HAD the archive --
which is why the probe passed and the build failed. Same package set, one
flag. FIX: name libclang-rt-dev explicitly in the apt line. Confirmed by a
30s probe with --no-install-recommends + libclang-rt-dev before rebuilding.
Also: requirements.txt has no platform-specific pins; the pip step never ran
in build #2. And the background-build wrapper now propagates the docker exit
code (build #2 reported exit 0 from the shell while docker had failed --
appended-to-log exit codes are not exit codes).
LESSON for the lab notebook: a probe must use the SAME flags as the build.

SANDBOX BUILD #3: SUCCESS. tofu-sandbox:latest, 1.91GB, "atheris+mcp import OK"
in-image. First smoke died at container START, not in the harness:
  runc: create mountpoint for .../eval/corpora_gpt41-sandbox: read-only file
  system
Docker needs the mountpoint DIRECTORY to exist inside the ro repo bind before
it can overlay onto it; the pre-existing dirs (targets/state/runs/...) mounted
fine, the arm-scoped ones (corpora_$ARM, metrics_$ARM) did not exist on the
host. FIX: sandbox.sh now mkdirs both the sandbox-backed source AND an empty
host-side mountpoint per overlay; both gitignored (eval/sandbox/,
eval/corpora_*-sandbox/, eval/metrics_*-sandbox/). The host-side dirs stay
empty forever -- writes go through the overlay to eval/sandbox/<d>.

SANDBOX HARNESS BUG (mine) FIXED: uv installed into /root/.local + symlinked to
/usr/local/bin, but /root is mode 700 so the non-root `tofu` user got
"Permission denied" -> shutil.which("uv")=None -> EVERY per-target Python venv
skipped with "uv not installed". Dockerfile now copies the real uv binary to a
world-executable path (late layer -> atheris stays cached, ~30s rebuild).
Verified: uv 0.12.13, which(uv)=/usr/local/bin/uv as tofu.
Restart prepare WITH --retry-skipped so the uv-blocked python repos re-attempt
(they were written to skipped.jsonl). The other skips the user saw were
LEGITIMATE and match host classes: locallama ERR_DLOPEN_FAILED (native sqlite),
azure-devops/google-search missing API keys, mcp-starter needs a build step.
Node prepare already works in-sandbox (appium 5, excel 14, whistle 34 READY;
npm postinstall now runs as uid 1000, no host home).

