2026-09-12  SANDBOX MOUNT BUG (Docker Desktop same-path) + VIPER IMAGE
================================================================
Viper image (tofu-viper-sandbox, 3.37GB) builds fine: codeql 2.27.0 native
arm64, node22, viper venv, bundle ships javascript/python query libs (no
`codeql pack install` into ro repo). BUT the first viper smoke's "OK + 5 SARIF"
was STALE overlay data -- Viper could not actually read its own code.

ROOT CAUSE (cost several probes to isolate):
  Mounting the repo at its IDENTICAL host path (-v $REPO:$REPO) collides with
  Docker Desktop's auto-shared /Users and yields an EMPTY mount (container sees
  repo root as root:root 755, 0 files; Benchmarks = ENOENT). Intermittent --
  it worked for earlier ToFu prepare, then silently went empty after the
  daemon/session restart. `-v $REPO:/mnt` showed all 38 files, proving it is
  the TARGET PATH, not perms or sharing scope.
  ALSO a red herring chased first: Benchmarks/Viper-MCP was mode 700 (umask);
  chmod 755 did not help because the real issue was the same-path mount.

FIX: mount the repo at /work; bake a symlink in BOTH images so prepared.jsonl's
absolute paths still resolve:
  ARG REPO_PATH=/Users/nazmulislamananto/pseclab/ToFu
  RUN mkdir -p "$(dirname "$REPO_PATH")" && ln -sfn /work "$REPO_PATH"
  Verified as root: /work=38 files, node_hook.js READABLE via the symlinked
  abs path. sandbox.sh + viper_sandbox.sh mounts rewritten $REPO->/work,
  overlays ->/work/eval/*, -w /work. Rebuilding both images (symlink is a late
  layer -> atheris/codeql cached).

SEPARATE REAL BUG to fix after the mount lands (do NOT trust viper numbers
until then): the node runtime hook is NOT wired into server_launcher.py --
it calls inject_python_hook_env only (line 44); node injection lives in
_build_command via instrument+instrumentation_script, which the caller must
set. On host hook_injected=True, in sandbox it was False. Re-smoke after the
mount fix; if still False, wire inject_node_hook_env / pass instrumentation_
script=node_hook.js for node targets. hook=False => Viper reports static
candidates without runtime confirmation => HIGHER FP, not fewer findings.
   75. Re-smoke viper sandbox after rebuild; confirm node_hook.js loads
       (oracle.json non-empty, hook_init present) before any viper campaign.

