2026-09-12  BUG 23 (HARNESS SECURITY): fuzzed targets inherited our REAL API keys
================================================================
While wiring per-target env for credential-gated servers, found that
src/runners/js_runner.py built the child env as a bare os.environ.copy().
run_arm_*.sh sources .env, so every fuzzed server -- untrusted third-party
code -- has been running with our real OPENAI_API_KEY and OLLAMA_CLOUD_API_KEY
in its environment, on the host AND in the sandbox (sandbox.sh passes -e
OPENAI_API_KEY into the container; the target inherits it). An adversarial
server could have exfiltrated them. Verified both keys present in the env
targets receive. FIX: _scrub_secrets() in js_runner (exact-name set + suffix
pattern _API_KEY/_SECRET/_TOKEN/_PASSWORD/...) applied to the INHERITED env
before custom_env is merged, so deliberate placeholders still reach the
target; same scrub in prepare_targets.target_env(). LIMITATION: PythonRunner
imports the target in-process and shares os.environ with ToFu's own LLM
client, so python targets (8 of 41) still see the key; fixing that needs the
key popped after LLM selection/seedgen and before target import -- item 80.
   79. ROTATE OPENAI_API_KEY and OLLAMA_CLOUD_API_KEY (Ananto; item 46 was
