2026-09-13  *** PYTHON ARM SILENTLY BROKEN -- PythonRunner tool discovery ***
================================================================
gpt41-Acodeql run (Set A ∩ CodeQL-flagged, 4 python repos, 25 configs):
INVALID. 23/25 never started the runner; 0 findings is NOT evidence.
  Bug A (18 configs, osm 12 + text-editor 6): prepare's detect_launch prefers
    the venv CONSOLE SCRIPT (.venv/bin/osm-mcp-server, args=[]). PythonRunner
    imports IN-PROCESS and has no .py/-m to work with -> falls to
    `module_name = self.command` -> importlib.import_module("<abs path to bin>")
    -> "No module named '/Users/.../eval/targets/<slug>/'". The bin path is not
    importable; the runner needs the MODULE (pyproject [project.scripts]
    "name = pkg.mod:func" -> import pkg.mod, call func) or must parse the shim.
  Bug B (5 configs, uml-mcp): loads server.py, then getattr(module,
    'generate_uml') -- but FastMCP registers tools via @mcp.tool() into the
    FastMCP instance's registry, NOT as a module-level callable. Runner must
    find the FastMCP/Server instance in the module and pull the tool fn from
    its registry (._tool_manager / list_tools) by name.
  Bug C (midi, 2): runner STARTED (llm=ok) but every input rejected
    ("Invalid chord name", "Cannot create property 'bpm' on string") -> seed
    type-quality (class b), midi stays in the denominator.
SIGNIFICANCE: Python is the ONLY arm where the 21 introspection tracers run
(Table 3 / RQ3 -- the paper's core contribution). PythonRunner failing to
start on the two most common FastMCP layouts means the python side has been
producing 0-findings-that-arent-evidence all along -- which explains why ALL
3 confirmed findings (V1 excel, V2 log-inj, V3 update) are NODE. Fixing this
is the single highest-value change left for finding python-side bugs.
   86. FIX PythonRunner.start() tool discovery: (A) resolve console-script ->
       module:function via pyproject [project.scripts] (prepare should emit the
       module, OR the runner should read the shim); (B) FastMCP registry lookup
       fallback when getattr(module, tool) fails. Validate in-sandbox on
       uml/osm/text-editor. Delicate (in-process import; bug-12 history) --
       test each step. This unblocks the entire python arm.

