2026-09-13  VM VIPER "ERR on all 41" -- ROOT CAUSE: committed prep state
================================================================
Symptom: every VM target ERR'd in ~4s, no fuzzer.log. Real cause (from
eval/viper_runs/<slug>.log, NOT <slug>/fuzzer.log which never got created):
  "Repo path not found: /Users/nazmulislamananto/.../eval/targets/graphlit..."
  "Cannot find module '/Users/.../dist/index.js'"
eval/state/prepared.jsonl was COMMITTED with the laptop's absolute paths, and
eval/targets is gitignored. So the VM clone had 41 "ready" targets pointing at
/Users/... that do not exist there; prepare_targets.py saw them as already_done
and skipped -> targets never cloned on the VM -> node launch fails instantly.
NOT a codeql or requirements problem (both verified fine on the VM).
FIX (repo, pushed 4eb1d5b): git rm --cached prepared.jsonl + skipped.jsonl,
gitignore them (machine-specific absolute paths, regenerate per host);
vm_bootstrap_viper.sh now `rm -f`s stale prep state before re-preparing.
FIX (VM, immediate): rm eval/state/{prepared,skipped,viper_runs}.jsonl +
eval/viper_runs/*, then prepare_targets.py --only-set host (clones+installs the
41 on the VM with VM paths), then re-run viper.
LESSON: absolute paths in committed state break cross-host reproduction. Any
state file with an abs path must be gitignored, not committed.

