================================================================
2026-09-15  ITEM 86 FIX: PythonRunner tool discovery + in-process isolation
================================================================
GROUND TRUTH before the fix (eval/state/runs.gpt41-full.jsonl): ALL 44 python
rows are `executable: unknown`, n_exec=0. Not ONE input ever executed on a real
Python target in any campaign. Every Python "0 findings" was non-evidence
(CLAUDE.md failure mode, at full scale). Per-run logs:
  39x "Failed to start runner: No module named '/Users/.../eval/targets/<slug>/'"
   5x "Could not find callable tool/function '<tool>' in module 'server'"
Item 86 named two causes; there were THREE:
  A. console-script PATH fed to importlib.import_module()  (osm, meilisearch,
     mindmap, text-editor: prepare emits .venv/bin/<script>, args=[]).
  B. FastMCP tools live in the server instance registry; uml-mcp resolves
     `mcp` lazily via module __getattr__ so dir(module) never lists it.
  C. (NEW) dependency isolation was impossible: ToFu = py3.11 + mcp 2.2.0 and
     src/fuzzer.py:13 `from .client import MCPInspector` pre-imports 107 mcp
     2.x modules; target venvs were py3.10-3.14 (uv honours each repo's
     .python-version / lock) with mcp 1.x. A cp313 pydantic_core cannot load
     into cp311, and `from mcp.server.fastmcp import FastMCP` (1.x API) can
     never resolve against the already-imported 2.x package.

FIX (src/runners/python_runner.py, rewritten start(); execute() unchanged but
for two compat lines):
  - console script -> parse the shim (`from X import Y`) or pyproject
    [project.scripts] -> import MODULE X, never call Y (it runs the server).
  - discovery: module globals -> explicit getattr for mcp/server/app/...
    (fires __getattr__) -> zero-arg factories (get_mcp_server, create_server,
    build_server...) -> walk sys.modules under the package prefix
    (osm_mcp_server.server.mcp). Matches class MRO names {FastMCP, MCPServer}
    so mcp 1.x FastMCP, mcp 2.x MCPServer, fastmcp 2-4, and subclasses
    (GeminiCompatibleFastMCP) all count; low-level handle = ._mcp_server OR
    ._lowlevel_server (2.x).
  - tool lookup from the registry (_tool_manager._tools / get_tools()); tools
    taking an MCP Context (osm's `ctx: Context`) are routed through the
    in-process JSON-RPC server instead of a bare call that could never
    supply ctx (would have been 100% rejects, class b).
  - target venv activation: site.addsitedir(<venv>/lib/pyX.Y/site-packages)
    (honours editable .pth) moved to the FRONT of sys.path + cwd + cwd/src;
    if the target ships its own `mcp`, purge mcp/mcp.* from sys.modules so
    ITS SDK version resolves (ToFu's already-bound MCPInspector objects are
    unaffected). Version mismatch -> RuntimeError naming both versions and the
    re-prepare command. LOUD, never silent.
  - predict_module_name(): fuzzer._start_runner consumed runner.module_name
    BEFORE start() set it -> the target package was never in atheris'
    instrument_imports(include=...) -> libFuzzer fuzzed every Python target
    blind. Now predicted without importing and added (top-level package).
  - mcp 2.x compat in the in-process JSON-RPC path: types.JSONRPCMessage is a
    bare Union alias there (no model_validate); build JSONRPCRequest /
    JSONRPCNotification directly. SessionMessage optional (mcp<1.8, osm 1.3).
  - get_tool_metadata() prefers the registry's own JSON schema.
  - src/fuzzer.py: PythonRunner gets cwd=target_cwd (bug 21, python side).
INTERPRETER DECISION: in-process => target venv MUST equal ToFu's CPython.
  atheris 3.0.0 supports 3.11-3.13 (atheris/version_dependent.py:37). Lock
  requires-python of the 8 sandbox python targets: uml >=3.12,<3.15; osm and
  mcp-text-editor >=3.13; replicate/markdownify >=3.11; mindmap/meilisearch/
  python-interpreter >=3.10. => 3.13 covers 8/8, 3.11 only 5/8.
  Dockerfile.sandbox: FROM python:3.13 + uv venv --python 3.13 +
  ENV TOFU_TARGET_PYTHON=3.13. Host dev venv stays 3.11 (tests only).
  eval/prepare_targets.py: TARGET_PYTHON defaults to the RUNNING interpreter
  (invariant is equality, not a constant); `uv sync --frozen --python
  $TARGET_PYTHON` (was unpinned -> picked 3.13/3.14 per repo); records
  "python" + "inprocess_ok" + "python_entry" in configs/prepared rows; new
  `--redo` (with --only-repo) re-prepares READY repos from scratch.
TESTS: tests/test_python_runner_discovery.py, 15 tests (shim/pyproject parse,
  venv helpers, mismatch raises loudly, interpreter-with-no-target is a clear
  error, registry/lazy-__getattr__/factory/subclass discovery, Context
