*** ATTRIBUTION MECHANISM, Python arm (RQ2/RQ3, attribution trap) ***
check_introspection_log_injection was NOT in the LLM selection
(['check_introspection_type_confusion','check_introspection_prototype_
pollution','check_introspection_redos']) and NOT in the 10 mandatory. It
fired anyway because fuzzer._run_sanitizers gates introspection checks as
   if "<check>" in self.selected_sanitizer_names or <tracer evidence>:
(seen on type_confusion/format_string/prototype_pollution/external_config/
fd_leak/deadlock/divide_by_zero/memory_access/unchecked_loop/cross_session
... -- counts of 'or'-gated vs selection-only gates recorded by grep in the
same session). CONSEQUENCE: on the Python arm every introspection check whose
tracer recorded anything runs regardless of selection -> an introspection
alert is NOT evidence that LLM selection mattered. V4's check_introspection_
sensitive_file_access was selected but would have fired unselected (its
tracer recorded /etc/passwd). V4/V5 write-ups say so explicitly.
FOR THE PAPER: RQ3 (introspection oracle finds bugs) is supported by V4/V5;
RQ2 (LLM selection precision matters) is NOT supported by them -- the
selection experiment must compare alert sets with the 'or <evidence>' path
disabled (or report only the string-sanitizer layer, where selection gates).
TO DOUBLE-CHECK: is this 'or evidence' behaviour Pierre's intent ("hybrid
architecture", fuzzer.py ~1117) or an accident? Ask before changing it; do
NOT flip it mid-campaign.
  EXACT (grep, 2026-09-15): src/fuzzer.py:743
    if "check_introspection_sensitive_file_access" in self.selected_sanitizer_names or acc_files:
  src/fuzzer.py:757
    if "check_introspection_log_injection" in self.selected_sanitizer_names or logged_msgs:
  38 introspection gates use `... in selected or <evidence>`; 4 are
  selection-only. So ~90% of the Python introspection layer is evidence-
  triggered regardless of the LLM.
