TOOLFUZZ SMOKE #2 (2026-09-15 16:28 VM): sync bridge works (server up, prompt
  set ran). New escape: `MCP error -32600: File not found: file path` -- a
  JSON-RPC error from excel-reader for a fuzzed path, raised as mcp McpError.
  ToolFuzz correctness.run_prompt catches ToolException ONLY -> whole tool ERR.
  FIX: make_sync() wraps every adapter exception as langchain ToolException.
  ORACLE CAVEAT FOR THE PAPER: ToolFuzz's runtime oracle = "tool raised". For
  MCP servers an error RESPONSE (isError / JSON-RPC error) is graceful input
  validation, not a crash. So ToolFuzz "runtime failures" on our corpus will
  mix (a) proper validation errors with (b) real breakage (server process
  died / transport closed / unhandled traceback in server stderr). At analysis
  time split by the recorded exception text: "MCP error -326xx" or isError =
  (a); "Connection closed" / BrokenPipe / timeout = (b). Only (b) is
  comparable to a ToFu crash-class alert. Do not report raw n_runtime_fail.
