  THE ONE REAL FINDING SO FAR (transport, 2 tools, 1 repo) -- TF-1:
    graphlit/graphlit-mcp-server (node, commit 1b94b88): sendTwitterNotification
    and sendEmailNotification kill the MCP SERVER PROCESS on any call when the
    provider env vars are unset. src/tools.ts: handler does
    `if (!consumerKey) { console.error(...); process.exit(1); }` -- 64
    process.exit(1) calls across ~34 tool handlers (all ingest*/list*/send*
    provider tools). A single tool call from any client = availability loss for
    the whole server (every other tool, every other session on that process).
    ToolFuzz saw it as ToolException(McpError: Connection closed) 5/5 on both
    tools. Why only 2 of the 34: 29 of the others hit the shared "Graphlit
    organization identifier is required" pre-check FIRST and return a graceful
    error; only the two notification tools check their own env before the
    org-id check. The other 32 kill-switches are reachable once an org id is
    configured -- i.e. in every real deployment. Confirmed by source, not by
    ToolFuzz's report.
    Cross-baseline on graphlit: Cisco 71 tools scanned, 0 findings. CodeQL 0.
    Viper: ok, rounds 10, n_anomalies 0, hook_injected False. MCPSafety: ERR
    (stale env, retry pending). ToFu: see next item.

  TO DOUBLE-CHECK -- INSTRUMENT GAP IN TOFU EXPOSED BY TF-1 (item 81):
    ToFu's sandbox run (findings/evidence/sandbox_triage_20260912, tofu_commit
    e14a363 -- PREDATES the Bug-20 fix 704f7fd) on the same two tools:
    n_exec=1, n_exec_success=0, exec_errors "Did not receive a matching
    response from JS process", then check_resource_exhaustion fired (10 and 54
    hits) and was triaged as FP under Bug 20. So ToFu OBSERVED the server die
    on the first call, did not restart it (1 exec, then 300-526 s of nothing),
    and MISCLASSIFIED the death as resource exhaustion. Post-Bug-20 ToFu would
    suppress the alert entirely -> silent miss of a real availability bug.
    Also: "Did not receive a matching response" is not in _TRANSPORT_FAILURES
    (src/fuzzer.py:896) -- check how _is_transport_failure catches it (res None?
    success flag?). ACTION (not done, needs Ananto's call):
      (1) new sanitizer class `server_terminated`: target process exits (or
          transport dies) DURING a tool call -> alert of its own class, with
          the call's args as witness. Distinct from resource_exhaustion.
      (2) JSRunner/PyRunner restart-on-death so fuzzing continues past the
          killing input instead of stalling to budget.
      (3) Re-run ToFu on graphlit after (1)+(2) -> expect 34 tools flagged
          once an org id is faked in env, 2 without.
    This is the disjoint-set thesis running the OTHER way: a baseline's oracle
    (tool raised -> "Connection closed") caught a class ToFu's oracle set does
    not model. Say so in the paper; it is the honest version of the comparison.
    Do NOT cite process.exit counts for other repos yet -- the corpus-wide grep
    (locallama 15, google-workspace 6, pluggedin 6, ...) counts ALL
    process.exit, mostly startup main(); only graphlit's are confirmed
    in-handler.

