2026-09-16  VIPER vs ToFu ANALYSIS + Viper pyql BROKEN (reference)
================================================================
Full writeup: findings/baselines/viper_vs_tofu_analysis_20260916.md.
Q: "we built ToFu to catch ANY vuln, why did it miss Viper's 12?"
A: Viper's 12 are NODE-only (jsql). Breakdown (source-verified):
  - 5 command-injection-from-request = ALL FALSE POSITIVES. Viper's query
    matches the method name ".exec(" and cannot tell RegExp.exec from
    child_process.exec:
      google-workspace gmail/patch.ts:100  /(\d\d?)…/.exec(dateHeader)  regex
      cursor10x index.js:3890              codeBlockRegex.exec(text)     regex
      knowledge-base mcp-resources.ts:107  /^kb:\/\/…/.exec(uri)          regex
      DesktopCommander open-browser.ts:29  execFile('open',[url]) /
                                           spawn('cmd',[..],{shell:false}) argv,no shell
    ToFu correctly stayed silent -> NOT misses.
  - 7 file-access-from-request = real path->read flows, ToFu blind spot:
      excel-reader x5 (readExcelFile/WorkbookCache/loadWorkbook): FORMAT-GATED.
        loadWorkbook parses xlsx; /etc/passwd -> throws -> no success -> silent-
        bug oracle can't fire. Also low-sev (can't exfil non-xlsx content).
        Contrast text-editor V4 (plaintext reader) which ToFu DID catch.
      cursor10x indexCodeFile x2: NON-EXECUTABLE in ToFu (13/18 tools need a
        project/DB context) -> no runtime data.
3 reasons ToFu misses a static-taint hit: (1) it's a Viper FP; (2) format/
  semantics gate blocks runtime success; (3) tool/repo not executable.
ToFu = dynamic, runtime-confirmed, high precision (bounded to reachable+
  success+modeled-sink BY DESIGN). Viper Phase-I = static taint, low precision
  here (5/12 FP). Complementary, neither subsumes.

*** Viper PYTHON taint is BROKEN in our setup ***
viper_runs.jsonl says the 6 host-python repos ran ok:true, but they produced
NO report.json. fuzzer.log: "Running CodeQL analyze with queries
['pyql/src/CommandInjectionFromRequest.ql', FileAccessFromRequest, Request
ForgeryFromRequest]" -> "CodeQL analyze failed with exit code 2" -> "Anchor
enrichment skipped: report not found". So the 6 python "0 vulns" = ANALYSIS
ERRORED, not clean. Viper's 12 are node-only.
  => comparison doc's "Viper: not run" on python is understated; precise
     reason = pyql analyze exit 2. DO NOT claim "Viper ran & missed V4/V6".
  95. (optional) fix Viper pyql exit-2 (query-pack / CodeQL-version), delete
      the 6 rows from eval/state/viper_runs.jsonl, re-run --only <repo> to get
      real python taint numbers. Only if we want a python Viper column;
      otherwise report "Viper python analysis errored" as a baseline limitation.
